    "feature_list": {
      "type": "feature-list",
      "blocks": {
        "feature_1": {
          "type": "feature",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/DSC2010_1.heic",
            "heading": "Myth: Creatine causes bloating",
            "content": "<p><strong>THE TRUTH: </strong>Creatine \"bloating\" is the result of increased muscle hydration. The \"bloating\" is most common during a loading phase. Our gummies are designed to be taken without loading.</p>"
          }
        },
        "feature_2": {
          "type": "feature",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Infographic_HowDoesCreatineWork_OrangeBG-min_1.png",
            "heading": "Myth: Creatine is not safe",
            "content": "<p><strong>THE TRUTH: </strong>In 2020, the FDA gave creatine monohydrate a GRAS Rating (Generally Regarded as Safe), putting it in the same safety category as Vitamin C and Whey Protein. It's also the most researched fitness supplement on the market with over 700 peer reviewed studies. Creatine is essential for the body!</p>"
          }
        },
        "feature_3": {
          "type": "feature",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG_8230_1.heic",
            "heading": "Myth: Creatine is only for men",
            "content": "<p><strong>THE TRUTH: </strong>Creatine is a beneficial for both men and women. Creatine's benefits are broadly desirable for anyone that lives an active lifestyle -- male or female. Did you know that over half of Create's customers are women?</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "feature_1",
        "feature_2",
        "feature_3"
      ],
